WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:00.260 --> 00:03.920
Congratulations — we've reached the end
of the problem-solving course.

2
00:03.920 --> 00:07.109
I know Emily and I have really enjoyed
this journey with you.

3
00:07.109 --> 00:12.023
We began by thinking about what problem solving is,
and about the process of making decisions.

4
00:12.023 --> 00:15.160
We talked about the different approaches to problem solving,

5
00:15.400 --> 00:19.963
and we spent a lot of time on the
hypothesis-led problem-solving approach:

6
00:19.963 --> 00:25.327
how we define the problem, how we structure it,
all the way to driving recommendations.

7
00:25.327 --> 00:29.150
One thing we hope you've taken away from this course is that —

8
00:29.510 --> 00:34.910
there is a structured approach, but it's less about
going through each of the steps one by one,

9
00:34.910 --> 00:39.457
and more about how you can apply it for yourself
and for your team's day-to-day.

10
00:39.457 --> 00:43.550
You've had some opportunities to think about that
throughout the course.

11
00:43.620 --> 00:48.790
Now, going forward, this is the opportunity to think about
how you apply this Monday morning.

12
00:48.790 --> 00:51.514
I couldn't agree with Marc more. Congratulations.

13
00:51.514 --> 00:56.740
This is one of the foundational pillars of what will make you
an even more exceptional leader.

14
00:57.350 --> 00:59.750
But remember, this is just one of the pieces.

15
01:00.170 --> 01:07.130
Getting beyond the paper, moving beyond the recommendation —
really thinking about how to keep it simple,

16
01:07.130 --> 01:15.680
practical and easily executable — these are the core things
you'll need to do to realise the true impact of your problem solving.

17
01:16.070 --> 01:19.330
Congratulations, have fun,
and get out there and practise.
